[{:db/id "q-69962/selection/6e66a03c3a2b05a882e15534a6f4d8260b30e940d02186b3f3f082cceff9aa91" :answer/id #uuid "cafd4c5f-f8c0-5d64-b5c4-9c9b9b319f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4.069)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4.069))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69962/selection/52028f12b5bff1e2ad790fd37c736f229d6e12bb194cc5a82fbee57835ab7482" :answer/id #uuid "862bd1f5-92ef-5bab-9714-4c3cd82e33a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4.069)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4.069))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69962/selection/2ee9129f4c36ef6711827cf52232615b58f9a91f59bcfef17aaf4599c47349d8" :answer/id #uuid "4e119664-0faa-5cd5-841b-9396d5a4cb60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3.927)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3.927))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69962/selection/66455bb45eb2824980aa986c2ff447a855261dcb2252872dc66b63dc463d3502" :answer/id #uuid "55c6c018-08a6-59ee-aec7-9670fe057069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2.214)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2.214))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69962/selection/44e31b133728a1e0a3b690aaa5225c26e82ebec92efd638420b67e0cc61d71e3" :answer/id #uuid "f7112fc0-125f-517f-9bf3-2ea36bcb588d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2.214)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2.214))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69962/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "95aa8638-5aa9-59f2-980a-3f397851a4ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-69962/selection/52028f12b5bff1e2ad790fd37c736f229d6e12bb194cc5a82fbee57835ab7482" :answer-field/choices ["q-69962/selection/6e66a03c3a2b05a882e15534a6f4d8260b30e940d02186b3f3f082cceff9aa91" "q-69962/selection/52028f12b5bff1e2ad790fd37c736f229d6e12bb194cc5a82fbee57835ab7482" "q-69962/selection/2ee9129f4c36ef6711827cf52232615b58f9a91f59bcfef17aaf4599c47349d8" "q-69962/selection/66455bb45eb2824980aa986c2ff447a855261dcb2252872dc66b63dc463d3502" "q-69962/selection/44e31b133728a1e0a3b690aaa5225c26e82ebec92efd638420b67e0cc61d71e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69962" :question/id #uuid "96f50b9f-4314-5efd-bcd6-b43eb0c3fc46" :question/math-academy-id "q-69962" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{10}{-3+4\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give $\\theta $ in radians to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $-3-4\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{10}{-3+4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(-3-4\\text{i})}{((-3)+4\\text{i})((-3)-4\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(-3-4\\text{i})}{(-3)^{2}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-30-40\\text{i}}{9+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{30}{25}-\\frac{40}{25}\\text{i} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{5}-\\frac{8}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=-\\frac{6}{5}-\\frac{8}{5}\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{6}{5})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{8}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{100}{25}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=-\\frac{6}{5}$ and $y=-\\frac{8}{5}$ are both negative, $z$ lies in the third quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{(-\\frac{8}{5})}{(-\\frac{6}{5})}| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & ≈4.069,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. \n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4.069)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4.069))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-69962/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69962"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107509/selection/b302ff60007153df243286a09d1714bcdfda76f80124434455e9fa4cc43fc669" :answer/id #uuid "02835dbb-6f6e-59bd-a5ad-8db1fdb8ecbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107509/selection/c1572fd942f7819a72901dd7d4a0de708c2a6233b973732ccc010108bfa540d6" :answer/id #uuid "558486eb-ee9a-5301-a7c4-5c9bd4ec8a09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107509/selection/001e7043103fb6e9f4976437993dcfe7eb9e7810a65c446a351bd0bca1032ef6" :answer/id #uuid "24884dec-1f51-506d-ae2d-52775d2f3289" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107509/selection/a83c7121082e1fade89b211adf31944bcbb5eaf1a3106389900c984d1e917269" :answer/id #uuid "a6d989db-3492-5ed7-a98b-1580b2719cd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107509/selection/1ccb34020688903eda8746f6739c35e8612f5ffed25d25a8735c0ed480c4013f" :answer/id #uuid "be2f8ad8-b28d-5ab1-971f-501681e267f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107509/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bac8ce53-9387-5f15-91f9-805dc5eaf213" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107509/selection/a83c7121082e1fade89b211adf31944bcbb5eaf1a3106389900c984d1e917269" :answer-field/choices ["q-107509/selection/b302ff60007153df243286a09d1714bcdfda76f80124434455e9fa4cc43fc669" "q-107509/selection/c1572fd942f7819a72901dd7d4a0de708c2a6233b973732ccc010108bfa540d6" "q-107509/selection/001e7043103fb6e9f4976437993dcfe7eb9e7810a65c446a351bd0bca1032ef6" "q-107509/selection/a83c7121082e1fade89b211adf31944bcbb5eaf1a3106389900c984d1e917269" "q-107509/selection/1ccb34020688903eda8746f6739c35e8612f5ffed25d25a8735c0ed480c4013f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107509" :question/id #uuid "21987eb4-af11-5168-90a9-e1154ee11ffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-107509" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}}{\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $\\sqrt{3}-\\text{i}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}}{\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})(\\sqrt{3}-\\text{i})}{(\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i})(\\sqrt{3}-\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}+2\\text{i}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i})}{3+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\frac{\\text{i}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\frac{\\text{i}}{2},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ are both positive, $z$ lies in the first quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107509/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107509"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107578/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "ed4e842d-4ded-5a52-9282-33744cf14061" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107578/selection/d0a25a5ffd46ca3d3da60ca4de3ef7a2e208ea13eada529c7dd4444c31402c16" :answer/id #uuid "629c12ad-41a1-52a2-93a0-3a5c3796eda7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107578/selection/6115cec4c91996e51c6f66aac3fdd66c7ac2a5d2d6833fb5c44157bd1ea74b91" :answer/id #uuid "a49c69df-689b-556f-aff9-b9a149296491" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107578/selection/99881be98e1e2d7d2100adcc918f854cf5ce3a3787a46c8c542e2f0dbc2d5842" :answer/id #uuid "1593a11a-251c-572a-ac6c-ef0eb2a8f006" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107578/selection/7205cb230b5fb3d2a31d422eb6126305074cb7029825ca23962a5eae727f07ed" :answer/id #uuid "169aef04-bb96-5ebb-bc88-5f75469e98a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107578/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "837eb07b-5e25-5899-96ed-b847a2be5f3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107578/selection/6115cec4c91996e51c6f66aac3fdd66c7ac2a5d2d6833fb5c44157bd1ea74b91" :answer-field/choices ["q-107578/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-107578/selection/d0a25a5ffd46ca3d3da60ca4de3ef7a2e208ea13eada529c7dd4444c31402c16" "q-107578/selection/6115cec4c91996e51c6f66aac3fdd66c7ac2a5d2d6833fb5c44157bd1ea74b91" "q-107578/selection/99881be98e1e2d7d2100adcc918f854cf5ce3a3787a46c8c542e2f0dbc2d5842" "q-107578/selection/7205cb230b5fb3d2a31d422eb6126305074cb7029825ca23962a5eae727f07ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107578" :question/id #uuid "67acef64-0c00-56f1-9f5c-f5da0c774591" :question/math-academy-id "q-107578" :question/problem "Express $z=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))$ in the form $z=x+\\text{i}y.$" :question/worked-solution "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=0$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =3(0-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107578/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31e4455a-9f8f-5c12-8c96-bb6735691591"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275076/field-1/e37f4ce5b7617223a46901d43c3aaec33db8b9fd888875eb3edae34de1222f5f" :answer/id #uuid "4aaf06c9-38f9-5074-9b8e-586102f27c06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275076/field-1/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" :answer/id #uuid "c4e599f1-1056-54bd-a9eb-79ade5fb6214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275076/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "189f703e-912a-5656-b076-ba7dbbadb5e7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275076/field-1/e37f4ce5b7617223a46901d43c3aaec33db8b9fd888875eb3edae34de1222f5f" :answer-field/choices ["q-275076/field-1/e37f4ce5b7617223a46901d43c3aaec33db8b9fd888875eb3edae34de1222f5f" "q-275076/field-1/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275076/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "695489e4-dbc2-511c-97f1-165292c5a62a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275076/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "08624d9f-51af-5654-9a9f-a5dad154530a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275076/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-275076/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275076" :question/id #uuid "c4b4bf78-a993-5ab5-a980-65500e859de9" :question/math-academy-id "q-275076" :question/problem "Express $z=6\\sqrt{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}))$ in the form $z=x+y\\,\\text{i},$ where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers. Give the **exact** values of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-$\n{{field-2}}\n$i$" :question/worked-solution "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nFirst, we find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the values and expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =6\\sqrt{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}(-\\frac{1}{2}-\\text{i}\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\text{i}\\,\\frac{18}{2} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{3}-9\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275076/field-1" "q-275076/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31e4455a-9f8f-5c12-8c96-bb6735691591"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321311/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "14c64fd2-17d6-5677-8c43-79dd0874f35b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321311/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "067b08fc-81d8-512f-99c7-550168bc40b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321311/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-321311/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321311" :question/id #uuid "7730ea9c-e41c-5589-bc78-7c3b9ca96ff0" :question/math-academy-id "q-321311" :question/problem "Express $z=7(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))$ in the form $z=x+y\\,\\text{i},$ where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers.\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i$" :question/worked-solution "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =7(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =7(0+\\text{i}\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =7\\cdot 0+7\\cdot \\text{i} \\\\  & =7\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321311/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31e4455a-9f8f-5c12-8c96-bb6735691591"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321311"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
